id: pm-review-respond
title: Post recorded verdicts and gate unanswered review work
description: Batch response command and read-only status gate reuse the complete GitHub transport and round evaluation; extends the delivered per-item verdict command.
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-15T07:59:47.637Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-17T08:11:43.636Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-17T08:11:43.634Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-15T09:48:33.000Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "respond is dry-run by default; apply posts concise verdict-only inline replies with fixing SHA, no bot mentions or private data, and a finding-id marker deduplicates retries; optional resolve defaults off; Vote every unvoted known review bot issue comment, review body and thread comment; configurable bot list and notice classifier; notices down and review content including accepted refusal up; never vote humans; receipt lists every vote; status lists unvoted items, missing verdicts, missing replies and unresolved threads; reuses exact-head round completion and exits zero only when clear; complete pagination fails closed; HTTP fixture server and real temp trackers cover retries, privacy and partial failures; behavioural revert proofs for marker detection and both vote classifications; unchanged npm and Bun release gates; changelog regenerated; read-only pm-github PR 124 evidence"
parent: pm-review-epic
resolution: "Delivered by https://github.com/unbraind/pm-review/pull/12 (merge 49ab278dc12f, head 5a97a32bed85)"
expected_result: "respond is dry-run by default; apply posts concise verdict-only inline replies with fixing SHA, no bot mentions or private data, and a finding-id marker deduplicates retries; optional resolve defaults off; Vote every unvoted known review bot issue comment, review body and thread comment; configurable bot list and notice classifier; notices down and review content including accepted refusal up; never vote humans; receipt lists every vote; status lists unvoted items, missing verdicts, missing replies and unresolved threads; reuses exact-head round completion and exits zero only when clear; complete pagination fails closed; HTTP fixture server and real temp trackers cover retries, privacy and partial failures; behavioural revert proofs for marker detection and both vote classifications; unchanged npm and Bun release gates; changelog regenerated; read-only pm-github PR 124 evidence"
actual_result: "Merged at 2026-10-15T09:48:33Z; no readable required checks, so every completed head check run had to succeed, be neutral or be skipped; successful checks: CodeQL, CodeRabbit, codeql, test (22), test (26)"
comments[12]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-15T08:00:40.744Z",codex-agent,"No duplicate batch-response feature found. Reuse the paginated transport and exact-head round evaluator. Status audits imported decisions and all live threads/votes; an empty tracker cannot hide unresolved threads. Historical resolved manual replies do not require retroactive import. Reply markers bind finding id and applying account; plan all actions before writes, reject unsafe verdict text, and default thread resolution off. Config uses explicit bot-login and notice-pattern flags shared by respond/status."
  "2026-10-15T08:08:10.981Z",codex-agent,"HTTP regression suite passed 5/5. Behavioural revert proofs each failed the same HTTP regression as expected: disabling only marker recognition reposted a reply; making the vote classifier always positive failed the trial notice downvote assertion; making it always negative failed the substantive review upvote assertion. Original implementation restored after all three proofs. No real GitHub mutations were made."
  "2026-10-15T08:10:30.357Z",codex-agent,"Real packed CLI status exposed the pinned host result contract: explicit exit_code zero is rejected, although direct handler tests accept it. Clear status receipts now omit exit_code so the host exits normally; blocked receipts retain exit_code one. The existing round handler also emits zero on success and remains outside this feature scope; report this existing host integration gap for follow-up."
  "2026-10-15T08:12:31.396Z",codex-agent,"Packed CLI live proof passed against merged public pm-github PR 124: status complete=true with empty unvoted, undecided, unreplied and unresolved lists and exact-head review complete; respond dry_run=true and actions empty. Both commands exited zero. No apply was run against a real repository. Existing round success host-contract gap tracked separately as pm-review-round-exit-contract. Linked test runner default 120-second timeout was too short under shared-host load; rerunning with a 600-second budget."
  "2026-10-15T08:15:44.771Z",codex-agent,"Linked test execution passed 1/1 (5 tests, zero failures) with the 600-second budget; elapsed approximately 125 seconds. Preliminary full coverage passed 129/129 and all four dimensions at 100 percent. Full npm/Bun release gates run with fresh HOME, GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null, GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1 and npm_config_ignore_scripts=true to suppress shared Git prepare hooks; explicit release scripts and build still execute."
  "2026-10-15T08:16:08.310Z",codex-agent,"Count correction: the preliminary outer suite summary is tests=121, pass=121, fail=0, skipped=0. The earlier 129 count counted nested tooling fixture output twice. Coverage remains statements/branches/functions/lines=100/100/100/100 across 20 inventoried sources. Final gate receipts will use the outer runner summaries."
  "2026-10-15T08:27:30.610Z",codex-agent,"Full isolated npm run release:check passed on code commit 01e3278: outer tests 121/121, zero failures/skips; packed npm/npx and Bun/bunx acceptance 1/1; coverage statements/branches/functions/lines all 100 across 20 inventoried sources; duplication zero; production audit clean; identity, types, lint, docstrings, changelog, package and attestation checks passed. Starting the separate isolated Bun release gate with the same thresholds."
  "2026-10-15T08:37:31.037Z",codex-agent,"Both full isolated release gates passed on unchanged runtime code commit 01e3278: npm and Bun each passed outer suite 121/121 with zero failures/skips and packed consumer acceptance 1/1; all four coverage dimensions 100 across 20 sources, duplication zero, production audit clean, and every remaining release check passed. Final read-only packed CLI proofs again exited zero: pm-github PR 124 status complete and respond dry-run actions empty. Acceptance evidence is in docs/respond.md. No real apply, merge, publication, pin change or threshold change. Releasing claim for orchestrator verification; feature remains in progress and the separate round host-contract follow-up remains open."
  "2026-10-15T08:46:58.547Z",codex-agent,"Verified round 1 finding: hasReply currently compares only the finding marker, so changing the refusal reason or verdict suppresses a correction. Plan: fingerprint verdict, reason and fix commit; distinguish stale replies in status; append an explicit superseding reply; cover unchanged, changed-reason and legacy-marker cases with HTTP fixtures and record a behavioral revert proof."
  "2026-10-15T08:50:05.554Z",codex-agent,"Round 1 HTTP suite passed 7/7 via pm test. New regressions: respond HTTP changed reason is stale until exactly one superseding reply; unchanged decisions stay inert; respond HTTP legacy marker is stale and a changed fix commit requires a new reply. The original dry-run/fix/refusal regression now requires a superseding reply on verdict change. Typecheck, lint, docstring and zero-duplication checks pass at unchanged thresholds. Behavioral revert proof: changed only hasReply to discard the decision fingerprint before matching; node --test --test-name-pattern=\"respond HTTP changed reason\" test/respond.test.ts exited 1 (0 passed, 1 failed), because stale_replies was empty instead of containing the finding. Restored the exact original implementation immediately afterward. No remote replies or reactions were posted."
  "2026-10-15T08:51:11.265Z",codex-agent,"The first full release attempt stopped at build:test: SDK get returns a projection with optional title, incompatible with the full metadata marker input used by two test assertions. Corrected those assertions to read the current decision through the existing typed reviewItems reader. No runtime implementation change; rerunning complete npm and Bun release checks."
  "2026-10-15T08:59:31.649Z",codex-agent,"Round 1 complete on commit 656c0ea (runtime implementation 476d335): isolated npm run release:check and bun run release:check each passed 123/123 outer tests, zero failures/skips, plus packed npm/npx and Bun/bunx consumer acceptance 1/1. Coverage statements/branches/functions/lines remains 100/100/100/100 across 20 sources; duplication zero; identity, types, lint, docstrings, production audit, package, changelog and attestation checks passed. The test metadata correction also avoids capturing mutable fixture state across awaits; lint and build:test passed before the successful gate runs. The 7-test HTTP suite and the expected changed-reason revert failure are recorded above. No thresholds, pins or gate scripts changed. Existing concurrent applies still require serialization. No new PM CLI or SDK defect encountered. Claim released for orchestrator verification; item remains in progress."
